            "24. Several offences committed within 12 months - any three may be selected and charged together, even if not part of the same transaction - ss.209(a) ACJA; 153(i) ACJL Lagos; 216(a) ACJL Kano. 25. Several offences connected as part of the same transaction - all may be charged together - ss.209(c) ACJA; 153(iii) ACJL Lagos; s.218 ACJL Kano; Onubaka v R. 26. Offences with the same elements but constituted under different laws - may be charged and tried together under the different laws (e.g. false pretences under s.419 Criminal Code and advance fee fraud under the AFFA), though conviction/sentence may only be entered for one - s.212 ACJA; s.219 ACJL Kano; Elliot v COP (1960). 27. Doubt as to which of several offences a single act/series of acts discloses - may be charged in the alternative (e.g. stealing / criminal misappropriation / criminal breach of trust) - ss.214 ACJA; 220 ACJL Kano; Azie v The State (1973). 28. Acts individually innocuous/a lesser offence but a different offence in combination - the defendant may be charged and tried at one trial both for the offence the combined acts constitute and for any offence constituted by one or more of the acts singly - s.213 ACJA (e.g. enticing a woman into one's house on a",
