            "(iv) Rule against ambiguity and uncertainty - a charge/information violating any requirement of validity is bad for ambiguity, e.g. failing to clearly identify the defendant, the precise allegation, the law violated, or the offence - tied to the defendant's right to know the offence charged (s.36(6)(b) CFRN) - Okeke v IGP (1965).",
